<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Template for https://innioasis.app/notice.xml

  Announcements and public service notices shown to users of the app.

  The app shows one notice at a time on the Select Software card, chosen for
  what the reader is looking at or has logged for update reminders, and cycles
  through the other applicable notices on that card. Clicking the card (or the
  Notices entry in the sidebar) opens the notices page, which lists every
  active notice with no contextual narrowing. Read more there opens a notice's
  full Markdown body in the page; the card and cards only use the short
  <content>.

  Attributes on <notice>:
    id          required, unique. Give a new id to publish a notice again.
    persistent  boolean ("true" | "false", default: "false").
                If false, the notice can be dismissed without returning at next run.
                If true, the notice returns on every app launch even after dismissal.
                Dismissals follow notice ids, not the file: a changed feed shows
                its new notices while dismissed notices stay hidden.
    severity    info | warning | critical   (default: info)
    type        optional player_update | app_update. Chooses the system
                notification category; omission means an ordinary notice.
    from        optional posting date or timestamp: YYYY-MM-DD, or YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM
                (also :SS, or a space instead of the T). Shown on the notice as
                "Posted ...". The notice is shown on or after this time.
    until       optional, ISO date YYYY-MM-DD. Shown on or before this date. Not
                shown to users.
    platform    optional comma-separated platforms: mac,windows,linux. Omitted
                means every platform.

  Contextual targeting (all optional; each one that is set must match):
    models            comma-separated Y1,Y2,A5. Blank or missing = all models.
    device_type       comma-separated hardware revisions: A, B (Y1 has both;
                      "Type A" is accepted). A revision is never offered for a
                      model that has no revisions.
    firmware_repo     repository the notice is about, written as in
                      slidia_manifest.xml: "rockbox-y1/rockbox". Full GitHub
                      URLs are accepted, and * wildcards work. Offered when the
                      reader selects firmware from that repository, or has a
                      device logged for update reminders that runs it.
    firmware_version  comma-separated release tag(s): "v3.2.0", "v3.2.*", "*".
                      "*" means any release of that repository. The leading "v"
                      is optional. Offered when that tag is selected, or when a
                      logged device's last recorded install is that tag.

  A notice with none of the targeting attributes is for EVERYONE. It stays on
  the card's rotation regardless of selection and is always in every list.

  A reader has one context per device: the current Select Software selection,
  plus each device logged for update reminders (added in Settings or recorded
  by an install). A notice is offered on the card when it matches any of them,
  and the card orders notices by how specific the match is: firmware_repo,
  then firmware_version, then device_type, then models, then everyone. One
  notice is visible at a time and the applicable ones alternate.

  Child elements:
    <title>         required, short heading (the card's first line).
    <content>       required, the short text shown on the card. Plain text,
                    also accepts <body>.
    <full_content>  optional, the complete text shown after Read more in the
                    app's full notice view, written in Markdown (headings,
                    lists, **bold**, *italic*, `code`, fenced blocks, quotes,
                    horizontal rules, [links](https://...), and images such as
                    ![screenshot](https://...)). It is not used for the card
                    preview; that uses the short <content>. The app renders it
                    with Qt's Markdown engine, and the site renders the same
                    text on the notice's own page. Falls back to <content> when
                    omitted. May also be a full_content="..." attribute on
                    <notice>.
    <url>           optional, https:// URL behind the full notice's "Open page"
                    button. When the app is not in English the button opens
                    the page's Google Translate view so the notice reads in the
                    user's language. A URL that is only the bare site root is
                    ignored, and the button is hidden. <link> is accepted as an
                    alias.

  A notice is the way to warn about firmware that should not be installed on a
  particular hardware revision, or about a new revision older releases do not
  support: put the one-line warning in <content>, the full explanation and the
  affected revision in <full_content>, and the detail page in <url>. Read more
  opens the full notice inside the app, filling the notices page; it does not
  send the reader to the bare site root.
-->
<notices updated="2026-11-03">
  <!-- For everyone: no targeting attributes. -->
  <notice id="2026-10-25-example" persistent="false" severity="info" from="2026-10-25T09:00" until="2026-12-31">
    <title>Welcome to Updater CE</title>
    <content>Firmware is downloaded from the community catalogue. Keep your player charged and plugged in during an install.</content>
    <full_content>Firmware and community software are downloaded from the catalogue and installed with SP Flash Tool or MTKClient. Keep the player charged and plugged in for the whole install, and do not unplug it until the app says the install is complete.</full_content>
    <url>https://innioasis.app</url>
  </notice>

  <!-- Contextual: only for Y1 Type A units running firmware from
       rockbox-y1/rockbox. Appears when that firmware is selected for the
       device, or when such a player is logged for update reminders. -->
  <notice id="2026-11-03-rockbox-y1-typea-example" persistent="false" severity="warning" from="2026-11-03" until="2026-12-31" models="Y1" device_type="A" firmware_repo="rockbox-y1/rockbox" firmware_version="*">
    <title>Rockbox on Y1 Type A: check your build</title>
    <content>Builds before 0.5 do not start on Type A units sold after March 2026. Update to 0.5 or later before installing.</content>
    <full_content>Type A Y1 units sold after March 2026 ship with a bootloader that rejects older Rockbox builds. Install **Rockbox 0.5 or later**, or stay on Original Software.</full_content>
  </notice>

  <!-- For everyone as well, and persistent: returns on every launch. -->
  <notice id="2026-10-20-psa-usb" persistent="true" severity="warning" from="2026-10-20" until="2026-11-20">
    <title>Use a direct USB port</title>
    <content>Avoid USB hubs during an install. Some hubs drop the connection partway through.</content>
  </notice>
</notices>
